  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This issue has turned up quite a bit since the new update, at first I thought it was just on my end, but sometimes other people can hear it too, sometimes people can hear them talking just fine.\nBasically when someone's talking, their voice will stutter, or hang on a quick chunk of when they're talking, and either it will continue what they're saying after the stutter, or it will just miss a chunk of their sentence, and just stutter. Some people were suggesting that this only happens with a person with VR, and not on Desktop, but i'm not 100% sure that this is true. \nI've also had the stutter happen to myself as well, and just before it happened I noticed a moment of lag, like a buffer overflow or something, and then the people I was talking with immediately told me that I myself was stuttering while talking.\nMy guess is this kind of goes hand in hand with the player's voices cutting out and not being able to hear anyone talking, or certain people talk",
